# Admin theme — Phase 1 + Phase 2 guardrails

## Source of truth

- Tokens + rules: `admin.voxbulk.com/adim-web/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`
- CSS: `admin.voxbulk.com/adim-web/src/styles/design-system.css` (`--ds-*`)
- Shared components: `admin.voxbulk.com/adim-web/src/components/ui/`
- Visual reference: `telynx-settings-hub-main` (OKLCH palette, density)

## Phase 1 (done)

- Shell chrome: Sidebar/Topbar tokens/density.
- Home Dashboard rebuilt to reference `/dashboard`.
- Foundation: Button, Table, Tabs, Card/Panel, Badge, KpiCard, Progress, Separator, Sparkline.

## Phase 2 — Batch A (in progress): quick wins

Migrate thin legacy / Dashboard-shaped pages to `components/ui` + design-system. Keep logic/API unchanged.

| Batch A targets |
|-----------------|
| Analytics: `PlatformKpis`, `CostRevenue` |
| Orgs: `OrganisationDetail`, `ZoneOrganisations`, `IntegrationTestGroup` |
| Campaigns: `CampaignsHub`, `CampaignTemplates` |

Already largely on ui (polish only if touched): `Organisations`, `Categories`, `OnboardingAddCustomer`, `Agents`.

## Phase 2 — later batches (do not nibble)

| Batch | Focus |
|-------|--------|
| B | Org Control Center, OrganisationProfile, OnboardingServices |
| C | Operations (`ops-theme`, queues, running surveys/interviews) |
| D | Feedback polish, Compliance, Team/settings thin pages |
| E | Billing & Pricing tables |
| F | Dedicated islands — Support Disk, AI Team, Sales Team, Telnyx/Meta hubs, Partners, Email, WA Templates Hub, Products Hub, Connection Profiles |

## Rules for new / touched admin UI

1. **Use `components/ui` + design-system tokens only** — no new page-local palettes, hex colors, or one-off button/table CSS.
2. **Do not invent tokens** — if something is missing, add it to `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` + `design-system.css` first.
3. **Do not create new theme islands.**
4. **Do not “fix” Batch F islands** unless that batch is the task.
5. Keep existing **Sidebar + Topbar shell** (nav/RBAC/search).
6. Visual/structural changes only unless the task explicitly changes logic/API.

## Legacy CSS

`styles.css` still powers non-migrated pages. Prefer Tailwind/`components/ui` on migrated work; do not expand legacy class islands.
